{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>נשקו בר</b> — Behold: serve YHWH, corresponding to <b>על</b> [in] 'against YHWH.'" "<b>ונשקו בר</b> — Corresponding to <b>על משיחו</b>. Now the meaning of <b>בר</b> is like <b>מה ברי ומה בר בטני</b> ['what my son and what the son of my womb']. And so it is written: <b>בני אתה</b> ['You are My son']. And the custom of the nations in the world is to place their hands under the hand of the king, like the brothers of Solomon, or the servant under the thigh of his master, or to kiss the king. And this custom persists to this day in the land of India." "<b>ופן יאנף</b> — [It] returns to HaShem mentioned in the first verse. And if it is distant, like <b>תבלעמו ארץ</b> ['may the earth swallow them'], it does not return to the word <b>מי כמוכה באלים</b> ['Who is like You among the elim'], but rather to <b>אמר אויב</b> ['said the enemy']. And thus <b>והקימו את המשכן עד בואם</b> ['and they shall set up the tabernacle until they come']." "And some say: <b>כי נשקו</b> — from the root נשק ['weapon']. And the meaning is: equip a weapon of <b>בר</b>. And behold <b>בר</b> is like <b>ברי לבב</b> ['pure of heart']. And it should have been <b>בור</b> or it should be its corrected form <b>הבר</b> or <b>כלי הבר</b>." "<b>ותאבדו דרך</b> — You will be lost on account of the way, like <b>נובלת עליה</b> ['it falls upon it'], for it itself does not fall, but upon it things fall, for it is of the standing participles. And Rabbi Moses the Cohen said: <b>דרך</b> is like <b>מדרך כף רגל</b> ['treading of the foot sole']. And this is far-fetched, for it has no reason." "<b>כי יבער כמעט אפו</b> — A verb going out like fire burning a forest, like consuming fire, and the passive is lacking, for there is no need, for the heat of anger is likened to fire."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:13.362358427Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}